	'about_band_h' => 'The grounds and facilities',
	'about_band_p' => 'Across our eleven hectares, mostly covered by trees, visitors discover an uncluttered and orderly park landscape. The central gravel driveway connects to our reception building and small shop, where guests can purchase fresh morning bread, milk, and camping gas.',
	'about_h1' => 'About the park',
	'about_lead' => 'Nohara Holiday Park was established in 2004 on a former tree nursery in Wenlow Vale by Ingrid Halloran.',
	'about_lead2' => 'Spanning eleven hectares of mature woodland and meadow, the park balances touring pitches and timber lodges with dedicated natural conservation.',
	'about_s1_h' => 'Our founding story',
	'about_s1_p1' => 'In 2004, Ingrid Halloran acquired eleven hectares of former commercial tree nursery land at Ash Hollow Lane 1 in Wenlow Vale. Rather than clearing the saplings and mature stands for open rows, she decided to retain the young oak, ash, and hazel trees, arranging the park around their natural growth. The park began with just twelve gravel touring pitches nestled between the young tree lines. As the woodland matured over the following years, Ingrid expanded the touring capacity to thirty-six gravel pitches and added sixteen unpowered grass pitches along the meadow boundary.',
	'about_s1_p2' => 'In 2012, fourteen timber lodges were introduced among the deeper oaks, designed to blend quietly into the forest canopy. Today, Ingrid still walks the grounds every morning, ensuring the park maintains its founding balance between outdoor hospitality and woodland stewardship.',
	'about_s2_h' => 'The grounds and facilities',
	'about_s2r_p1' => 'Nearby stands our heated wash house, offering hot showers and laundry facilities. A scenic 2.4-kilometre walking trail loops through the mature oak wood, passing a freshwater pond where dragonflies and aquatic insects flourish. Speed on all interior roads is strictly capped at 8 km/h to protect strolling guests and wandering wildlife, while park quiet hours run from 22:00 to 07:00.',
	'about_s3_h' => 'Grounds layout and how to arrive',
	'about_s3_p1' => 'Entering via Ash Hollow Lane 1, you pass through our timber five-bar gate. Reception sits straight ahead, with gravel pitches 1 to 36 arranged in small leafy clusters among oak and ash stands. Meadow tent pitches 37 to 52 stretch south along the open grass boundary, while timber lodges 1 to 14 are sheltered along the northern forest border.',
	'about_s3_p2' => 'Drivers can reach us via the main Wenlow Vale valley road, following signs onto Ash Hollow Lane. Cyclists can access the park directly from the regional cycle path, which links straight to our meadow edge. Reception welcomes arrivals daily from 08:30 in season.',
