	'close_h' => 'Book a week at Nohara',
	'contact_a1' => 'Pitch arrivals commence from 13:00, and departing pitch guests must vacate their pitch by 11:00. For our fourteen timber lodges, check-in begins from 15:00, with departure requested by 10:00 to allow our housekeeping staff to prepare the rooms. Weekly stays run from Saturday to Saturday. Upon arrival at the entrance gate on Ash Hollow Lane, head warden Tobias Weller or on-duty wardens will greet your party, supply your key or pitch number, and guide your vehicle directly to your accommodation.',
	'contact_a2' => 'Every booking is secured with a 25% deposit, and reception holds reservations free for 48 hours while you finalise travel arrangements. The remaining 75% balance must be paid four weeks prior to your arrival date. We offer free cancellation up to fourteen days before your scheduled check-in, returning your deposit in full. If you need to make changes to your booking dates or guest numbers, contact Hana Kovač at reception by calling +00 31 6120 0841 or emailing hello@nohara-park.example.',
	'contact_a3' => 'Well-behaved dogs are welcome across our touring and camping pitches. To maintain a peaceful environment and safeguard local wildlife, all dogs must remain on a lead at all times while within the park grounds. Owners are asked to exercise their dogs along the 2.4-kilometre oak wood walking loop and clean up immediately after them. Dogs are not permitted to wander unattended, and we ask owners to respect park quiet hours between 22:00 and 07:00 so all guests enjoy restful sleep.',
	'contact_a4' => 'Our thirty-six gravel touring pitches feature dedicated 10A electric hook-up points suitable for caravans, campervans, and motorhomes. Fresh drinking water standpipes are located within thirty metres of every touring pitch. Please note that our sixteen meadow grass tent pitches are unpowered to preserve an open, traditional camping atmosphere. Guests staying on grass pitches can access electricity for phone charging and personal grooming in our heated wash house, which remains open throughout the day and evening.',
	'contact_a5' => 'Each timber lodge comes fully furnished with fresh bed linen and bath towels for every guest, a fully equipped self-catering kitchen, dining table, and an efficient wood-burning stove with firewood. Kitchens include cookware, crockery, cutlery, cooking stove, and refrigeration. Verandas are fitted with outdoor timber seating overlooking the woodland. Guests need only bring personal toiletries and groceries. Basic grocery essentials including fresh morning bread, milk, and bottled drinks can be purchased at our small reception shop during regular opening hours.',
	'contact_a6' => 'We provide winter storage for up to thirty caravans in our secure yard from November to mid-March for €320 per season. Warden Luca Ferreira oversees the storage area, carrying out weekly physical inspections of all caravan covers, corner steadies, and hitches. On dry winter days, caravans are aired to prevent dampness. Owners can arrange caravan collection by appointment during March when the new touring season opens, or choose to book a pitch week and stay immediately.',
