	'lodges_prices_h' => 'Lodge prices',
	'lodges_s1_h' => 'Two-bed and three-bed lodges',
	'lodges_s1_p1' => 'We offer ten two-bed lodges and four three-bed lodges, built from timber and positioned to overlook the quiet woodland floor. Two-bed lodges sleep up to four people across two comfortable bedrooms, making them ideal for couples and small families. Three-bed lodges sleep up to six guests, offering spacious shared accommodation for larger family gatherings.',
	'lodges_s1_p2' => 'Inside every lodge you will find a fully fitted kitchen, dining area, private bathroom, and an efficient wood-burning stove for cool evenings. Outside, a covered wooden veranda extends into the trees, providing sheltered space to sit outdoors. Fresh bed linen and bath towels are included with every booking.',
	'lodges_s2_h' => 'Lodge prices and short breaks',
	'lodges_s2_p1' => 'Lodge holidays primarily run by the week, with changeover taking place each Saturday. A seven-night stay in a two-bed lodge costs €690, while a seven-night stay in a three-bed lodge costs €860. During selected periods, we also offer short breaks in our two-bed lodges: a three-night weekend break running Friday to Monday, or a four-night midweek stay running Monday to Friday, each priced at €380.',
	'lodges_s2_p2' => 'Additional guests aged five and over are charged €6 per night, while children under five stay free of charge. A 25% deposit secures your reservation, the remaining balance is payable four weeks before arrival, and cancellation is free up to fourteen days before check-in.',
	'lodges_s3_h' => 'Arrival and housekeeping',
	'lodges_s3_p1' => 'Lodge guests are welcomed to arrive from 15:00 on their scheduled arrival day. We ask guests to vacate their lodges by 10:00 on the day of departure so warden Amara Osei and our housekeeping team have time to thoroughly air, clean, and make up each room. When you arrive at Ash Hollow Lane, reception staff or a warden will supply your lodge keys, provide a clear park map, and explain how the wood stove functions.',
	'lodges_s3_p2' => 'The park remains quiet and serene at night, supported by an 8 km/h vehicle speed limit and quiet hours from 22:00 to 07:00.',
	'newsletter_h1' => 'Letters from the park',
	'newsletter_lead' => 'Subscribe to receive seasonal dispatches from Nohara Holiday Park directly to your inbox.',
	'newsletter_lead2' => 'We send four thoughtful letters a year covering opening dates, pitch booking releases, and conservation work across our eleven hectares.',
	'newsletter_s1_h' => 'What we send',
	'newsletter_s1_p1' => 'We write one letter each season to share quiet news from our grounds in Wenlow Vale. In spring, our dispatch announces the opening of the touring season on 15 March, detailing meadow conditions, wash house updates, and Élodie Brun\'s upcoming Saturday pond walks. Summer letters share woodland wildlife observations along our 2.4-kilometre oak trail.',
	'newsletter_s1_p2' => 'In autumn, we announce the opening of next season\'s pitch week reservations on 1 December, allowing guests to secure their preferred dates early. In winter, we share updates on warden work, including Samir Haddad\'s hedge laying and Luca Ferreira\'s caravan storage yard.',
	'newsletter_s2_h' => 'Our privacy commitment',
	'newsletter_s2_p1' => 'We respect your time and personal inbox. You will receive exactly one letter a season, without sales promotions, third-party advertising, or frequent automated messages. You can unsubscribe at any time with a single click using the link at the foot of every email, and we never share, sell, or transfer your contact details to outside organisations.',
	'newsletter_s2_p2' => 'If you prefer to receive news by post or have questions about upcoming dates, you are always welcome to call reception on +00 31 6120 0841 or email hello@nohara-park.example.',
