	'out_of_season_h1' => 'Out of season',
	'out_of_season_lead' => 'From November to mid-March, Nohara Holiday Park enters its quietest months, dedicated to grounds maintenance, woodland conservation, and secure caravan storage.',
	'out_of_season_lead2' => 'Our timber lodges remain open throughout this peaceful period, offering tranquil winter breaks between the bare oak and ash trees.',
	'out_of_season_s1_h' => 'Winter grounds and woodland work',
	'out_of_season_s1_p1' => 'Out of season represents an essential working period for our wardens. During November and December, Samir Haddad and the team lay native hedges along Ash Hollow Lane, encouraging dense regrowth and protecting boundary wildlife. In January, the wardens carry out deep maintenance across the park drains and service the heated wash house.',
	'out_of_season_s1_p2' => 'February brings woodland conservation under founder Ingrid Halloran\'s guidance, including tree surveys, pruning, and coppicing across the 2.4-kilometre oak wood walk. In early March, Luca Ferreira and Samir re-gravel touring pitches and grade the access roads, ensuring all thirty-six gravel pitches stand in pristine condition for the 15 March opening.',
	'out_of_season_s2_h' => 'Winter caravan storage',
	'out_of_season_s2_p1' => 'Each winter from November to mid-March, we host winter storage for up to thirty touring caravans in our secure hard-standing yard. Luca Ferreira supervises the storage area, conducting weekly inspections of every caravan exterior and ensuring covers and hitches remain sound. On dry days each month, caravans are opened and aired to prevent condensation and dampness.',
	'out_of_season_s2_p2' => 'Winter caravan storage costs €320 for the full season. Owners can arrange collection by appointment during March when touring pitches re-open. Long-standing guests such as Greta and Paul have relied on our winter storage every September since 2011.',
	'out_of_season_s3_h' => 'Winter lodge stays',
	'out_of_season_s3_p1' => 'While pitches close during the colder months, our fourteen timber lodges stay open all year. Winter guests enjoy quiet woodland paths, frost on the branches, and peaceful evenings beside their lodge wood-burning stove. Two-bed lodges rent for €690 per week or €380 for short breaks running Friday to Monday or Monday to Friday, while three-bed lodges cost €860 per week.',
	'out_of_season_s3_p2' => 'Bed linen and bath towels are provided, and Amara Osei ensures fires can be lit promptly upon arrival. Reception remains open daily from 09:00 to 16:00 throughout winter, closing only on 25 and 26 December.',
