	'pitches_h1' => 'Touring pitches',
	'pitches_lead' => 'Nohara Holiday Park offers thirty-six hard-standing gravel touring pitches and sixteen unpowered grass tent pitches across eleven wooded hectares.',
	'pitches_lead2' => 'Set between mature oak and ash trees, each pitch enjoys natural seclusion and easy access to heated facilities.',
	'pitches_prices_h' => 'Pitch prices',
	'pitches_s1_h' => 'Gravel touring pitches',
	'pitches_s1_p1' => 'Our thirty-six gravel touring pitches are designed for touring caravans, campervans, and motorhomes. Each hard-standing pitch provides a generous ten by twelve metre level surface, leaving plenty of space for your vehicle, an awning, and outdoor seating. Every gravel pitch includes a dedicated 10A electric hook-up connection, and a fresh drinking water point is located within thirty metres.',
	'pitches_s1_p2' => 'Pitches are spaced naturally between trees originally planted when the grounds were a tree nursery. A gravel touring pitch costs €34 per night for two adults, one car, and your caravan or motorhome. A full seven-night pitch week running Saturday to Saturday costs €210.',
	'pitches_s2_h' => 'Meadow grass pitches',
	'pitches_s2_p1' => 'Along the open boundary of our park lie sixteen grass pitches reserved for tents and small campervans. These unpowered meadow pitches offer peaceful countryside views and a softer, traditional camping ground. Grass tent pitches cost €24 per night for two adults and one car. Additional guests aged five and over are welcome across all pitches for €6 per night, while children under five stay free.',
	'pitches_s2_p2' => 'Campers have unrestricted access to our heated central wash house, clean washing-up sinks, and the small reception shop stocked with fresh bread, milk, and gas. The open meadow edge is especially popular with walking and cycling travellers.',
	'pitches_s3_h' => 'Pitch arrival and park rules',
	'pitches_s3_p1' => 'Pitch check-in begins at 13:00, and we request that departing guests vacate their pitches by 11:00. When you arrive at the timber gate, Tobias Weller or Luca Ferreira will meet you, guide your vehicle along the gravel roads, and assist in backing your caravan onto your numbered pitch. A 25% deposit secures your pitch reservation, with the balance due four weeks before arrival and free cancellation up to fourteen days before your stay.',
	'pitches_s3_p2' => 'To ensure comfort for everyone, vehicles must not exceed the 8 km/h park speed limit, quiet hours apply between 22:00 and 07:00, and dogs must remain on a lead.',
