	'stays_h1' => 'Stays',
	'stays_h2' => 'Stays this season',
	'stays_lead' => 'Nohara Holiday Park offers fifty-two pitches and fourteen timber lodges set across eleven hectares of quiet woodland in Wenlow Vale.',
	'stays_lead2' => 'Whether you arrive with your own caravan, pitch a tent along the meadow, or move into a warm lodge with beds already made, our wardens ensure your stay is peaceful and unhurried.',
	'stays_more' => 'Prices and dates →',
	'stays_s1_h' => 'Every way to stay',
	'stays_s1_p1' => 'The park provides three distinct ways to stay between the oak and ash trees. We keep thirty-six gravel touring pitches with electric hook-up, sixteen grass tent pitches beside the meadow edge, and fourteen cedar-clad timber lodges nestled deeper in the woodland. Touring and tent pitches operate from 15 March until 2 November, welcoming caravans, motorhomes, and campers throughout the warmer months.',
	'stays_s1_p2' => 'Our timber lodges remain open all year round, providing heated self-catering accommodation through crisp autumn weeks and quiet winter weekends. Every stay includes full access to our heated wash house, the central pond, and the 2.4-kilometre oak wood walking loop.',
	'stays_s2_h' => 'Pitch and lodge options',
	'stays_s2_p1' => 'Each gravel pitch measures ten by twelve metres, giving ample room for a car, an awning, and a caravan or motorhome. These hard-standing pitches include a 10A electric hook-up connection and a fresh water standpipe within thirty metres. For traditional campers, our sixteen grass tent pitches sit along the natural meadow boundary without electricity, preserving open views across the grassland.',
	'stays_s2_p2' => 'Our ten two-bed lodges sleep up to four guests, while our four three-bed lodges accommodate up to six guests in comfort. Inside the lodges, freshly laundered bed linen and bath towels are provided for all beds, alongside a wood-burning stove and a fully equipped kitchen.',
	'stays_s3_h' => 'Arrival times and park life',
	'stays_s3_p1' => 'Pitch guests are welcomed from 13:00 on their day of arrival and depart by 11:00 on their final morning. Lodge check-in begins at 15:00, with departures scheduled by 10:00 so Amara Osei and our housekeeping team can prepare the rooms. Weekly reservations run from Saturday to Saturday throughout the year. When you pull up at the reception gate, head warden Tobias Weller or a fellow warden meets your vehicle and walks you directly to your pitch.',
	'stays_s3_p2' => 'To preserve the calm atmosphere of Wenlow Vale, vehicle speeds are strictly limited to 8 km/h, and quiet hours are observed park-wide from 22:00 until 07:00.',
	'stories_h1' => 'Guest stories',
	'stories_lead' => 'Guests return to Nohara Holiday Park year after year for the unhurried quiet of the trees and our wardens\' personal care.',
	'stories_lead2' => 'Here are four genuine accounts from visitors who spent their holidays touring, camping, and resting in our lodges.',
	'stories_s1_h' => 'The Abara family',
	'stories_s1_p1' => 'The Abara family arrived in early July for their very first week touring in a caravan. Having driven through Wenlow Vale with two young children, they were relieved when head warden Tobias Weller met them at the timber entrance gate. Tobias walked them along the gravel drive to gravel pitch 14 and patiently helped them back the caravan into place between the ash trees.',
	'stories_s1_p2' => 'Over the following seven days, the children joined warden Élodie Brun for the Saturday pond morning, collecting pond skaters and water beetles with nets, while the parents relaxed under their awning in the afternoon sunshine.',
	'stories_s2_h' => 'Greta and Paul',
	'stories_s2_p1' => 'Greta and Paul have visited Nohara Holiday Park every September since 2011. They reserve a gravel pitch week from Saturday to Saturday, enjoying the turning autumn colours along the 2.4-kilometre oak wood trail and quiet evenings on pitch 8. At the end of their stay, rather than towing their caravan home for winter, they hand it over to warden Luca Ferreira for winter caravan storage.',
	'stories_s2_p2' => 'Luca parks the caravan in our secure storage yard, inspecting it each week and airing it monthly until Greta and Paul return to collect it the following March when the new season begins.',
	'stories_s3_h' => 'The Lindqvist-Moreau family',
	'stories_s3_p1' => 'During October half-term, the Lindqvist-Moreau family booked a full week in one of our four three-bed timber lodges. Bringing three generations together under one roof, the grandparents, parents, and two children found ample room across the three comfortable bedrooms. Evenings were spent gathered around a long wooden table set on the covered veranda, dining under blankets in the brisk autumn dusk while listening to the wind through the oak canopy.',
	'stories_s3_p2' => 'With the wood-burning stove keeping the living room warm and beds prepared on arrival by Amara Osei, their stay provided a calm, restful family holiday.',
	'stories_s4_h' => 'Nadia and Kofi',
	'stories_s4_p1' => 'Nadia and Kofi arrived on two touring bicycles on a clear Tuesday afternoon in mid-May. Having cycled through Wenlow Vale via the regional cycle path, they chose an unpowered grass tent pitch along the meadow edge. They stayed for four peaceful nights, using their camp stove for morning coffee and enjoying unobstructed views across the wildflowers.',
	'stories_s4_p2' => 'Because vehicles are kept to 8 km/h and quiet hours begin at 22:00, they enjoyed undisturbed sleep each evening. After warm showers in our heated wash house and fresh rolls from the reception shop, they packed their panniers and continued their journey refreshed.',
	'story_cap' => 'Ingrid Halloran on the oak wood walk, 07:10',
	'story_h2' => 'A park that is walked every morning',
	'story_link' => 'Meet the wardens →',
	'story_p1' => 'Ingrid Halloran founded the park in 2004 on the grounds of a former tree nursery in Wenlow Vale. Rather than clearing the land for open lines of vehicles, she kept the mature oak and ash trees where they stood, setting the first pitches into natural clearings so every pitch would have canopy, shelter, and green space.',
	'story_p2' => 'Every morning begins well before the gates open at 08:30. Tobias Weller walks the gravel circuit at dawn, checking the water points, inspecting the 10A electrical hook-ups, and visiting the pond while mist still hangs above the reeds. By the time reception opens, every pitch is swept and ready for new arrivals.',
	'story_p3' => 'When guests reach the gate, a warden meets them in person to walk them to their pitch. Tobias backed the caravan on with the Abara family during their first caravan week, while their children later explored the pond with Élodie. That steady, unhurried care remains the rule for every stay.',
