	'wardens_band' => 'Seven people, eleven hectares',
	'wardens_h1' => 'The wardens',
	'wardens_lead' => 'The seven wardens and staff at Nohara Holiday Park look after eleven hectares of woodland, fifty-two pitches, and fourteen lodges.',
	'wardens_lead2' => 'From morning grounds patrols to Saturday pond sessions, our team maintains the park with quiet care and direct practical knowledge.',
	'wardens_note_c' => 'Ingrid Halloran, founder',
	'wardens_note_q' => 'I still walk the oak wood every morning, before the gates open. It is how I know what the park needs that day.',
	'wardens_ppl_l' => 'Read about the park →',
	'wardens_s1_h' => 'Grounds and woodland team',
	'wardens_s1_p1' => 'Ingrid Halloran founded Nohara Holiday Park in 2004 on a former tree nursery and still walks the 2.4-kilometre oak wood path every morning at dawn. Head warden Tobias Weller manages daily operations, inspects water and electrical hook-up points, and personally walks new guests to their pitches. Warden Samir Haddad cares for the trees, woodland hedges, and seasonal drainage across our eleven hectares, leading hedge laying and winter coppicing.',
	'wardens_s1_p2' => 'Warden Luca Ferreira looks after the thirty-six touring pitches, maintains electric connections, and oversees winter storage for up to thirty caravans from November to mid-March.',
	'wardens_s2_h' => 'Guest care and reception',
	'wardens_s2_p1' => 'Warden Amara Osei manages the fourteen timber lodges, overseeing housekeeping and making sure linen, towels, and firewood are prepared for every arrival. Hana Kovač manages reception and bookings, answering visitor enquiries within one working day, taking telephone calls, and handling the 48-hour reservation holds. Warden Élodie Brun organizes park activities, leading popular Saturday morning walks along the oak loop and pond exploration sessions where children discover aquatic insects and pond life.',
	'wardens_s2_p2' => 'Working alongside one another, our seven-person team ensures that guests experience a welcoming, orderly, and peaceful environment throughout their stay in Wenlow Vale.',
	'wardens_s3_h' => 'Our daily rounds',
	'wardens_s3_p1' => 'Every day begins early at Nohara Holiday Park. Before reception opens at 08:30 in season, Tobias Weller completes his dawn circuit of the grounds, checking every water post, testing pitch electrical boxes, and inspecting the heated wash house. Samir and Luca monitor the road surfaces and tree canopy, while Amara checks the lodge verandas.',
	'wardens_s3_p2' => 'When new arrivals pull in from 13:00 for pitches and 15:00 for lodges, a warden is always available at the gate. By upholding quiet hours from 22:00 to 07:00, our team preserves the unhurried woodland atmosphere that guests have valued since 2004.',
);
